[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5032053249","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121587#issuecomment-5032053249","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121587","id":5032053249,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABK-8KAQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T08:58:39Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T08:58:39Z","body":"Possibly related:\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113681","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5032053249/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5041246164","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121587#issuecomment-5041246164","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121587","id":5041246164,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLHtP1A","user":{"login":"LJYC-ME","id":93019192,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYtcOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93019192?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME","html_url":"https://github.com/LJYC-ME","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LJYC-ME/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T02:47:00Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T02:47:00Z","body":"I investigated this with RenderDoc, and the issue appears to come from negative alpha values produced by `blend_sub`.\n\nWhen an opaque subtractive sprite is drawn over transparent space, both RGB and alpha can become negative. The non-HDR UNORM target clamps these values to zero, while the HDR floating-point target preserves them.\n\n`CanvasGroup` first renders its children into the render target's shared backbuffer. It then draws the group owner back to the main target using the default shader and the default `blend_mix` state. The shader does not clamp negative alpha, so negative RGB and alpha values can pass through to the fixed-function blend stage. Since `blend_mix` multiplies the source RGB by the source alpha, negative RGB multiplied by negative alpha produces a positive contribution, causing the visible bright area.\n\nAs a project-side workaround, assigning a custom `ShaderMaterial` to the `CanvasGroup` and preventing negative alpha fixes the artifact:\n\n```glsl\nshader_type canvas_item;\nrender_mode unshaded;\n\nuniform sampler2D screen_texture :\n        hint_screen_texture,\n        repeat_disable,\n        filter_nearest;\n\nvoid fragment() {\n    vec4 c = textureLod(screen_texture, SCREEN_UV, 0.0);\n\n    c.a = max(c.a, 0.0); //[+] Prevent negative alpha from being used as the source blend factor.\n\n    if (c.a > 0.0001) {\n        c.rgb /= c.a;\n    }\n\n    COLOR *= c;\n}\n```\n\nI am also interested in following further discussion about the intended blending and compositing behavior.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5041246164/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5048468061","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121587#issuecomment-5048468061","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121587","id":5048468061,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLOmCXQ","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T16:01:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T16:01:49Z","body":"Thanks! A couple of things to consider: subtract is just a math operation: it doesn’t really have an absolute intent behind it. Also, alpha is just data: it’s often used for transparency but sometimes used for other things.\n\nThis makes it hard to reason about what intended behaviour should be…","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5048468061/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5049148673","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121587#issuecomment-5049148673","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121587","id":5049148673,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLPPlAQ","user":{"login":"finian1","id":38808702,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4ODA4NzAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38808702?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1","html_url":"https://github.com/finian1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finian1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T17:08:44Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T17:11:36Z","body":"> This makes it hard to reason about what intended behaviour should be…\n\nEither way, I believe behaviour should be consistent across both settings. Due to 2D HDR being off by default, I would argue that the first behaviour should be maintained in order to reduce the chance of breaking projects that rely on it. \n\nPersonally I also find the first behaviour more useful, as it allows for simpler masking within CanvasGroups without having to worry about the mask appearing in places where it shouldn't.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5049148673/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]